# Third-party software in VibeLC

VibeLC is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (`LICENSE`).
It uses:

- **libmpv** (<https://mpv.io>) for playback, under the GNU GPL version 2 or later, with FFmpeg
  (LGPL 2.1+), libass (ISC), libplacebo (LGPL 2.1+), dav1d (BSD-2-Clause) and LuaJIT (MIT). It is
  built from the upstream releases named in the VibeLC source: on Linux into the package's
  `libmpv.so.2` by `packaging/linux/build-libmpv.sh`; on Windows linked into `vibelc.exe` by
  `packaging/windows/build-libmpv.sh`, there also with FreeType (FreeType License), FriBidi
  (LGPL 2.1+), HarfBuzz (MIT), zlib (zlib License), shaderc, glslang, SPIRV-Tools and SPIRV-Cross
  (Apache 2.0, glslang also BSD-3-Clause), and the LLVM runtime libraries libc++ and libunwind
  (Apache 2.0 with LLVM exception) and mingw-w64 (ZPL and public domain).
- **Inter** (<https://rsms.me/inter>), SIL Open Font License 1.1 (`OFL-Inter.txt`).
- **Lucide** icons (<https://lucide.dev>), ISC License (`LICENSE-lucide.txt`).
- The Rust crates below, compiled into the program.

